WEBVTT

00:06.777 --> 00:09.287
Fatima. I want you...

00:10.107 --> 00:12.867
to act as my spy.

00:15.707 --> 00:17.097
Your spy?

00:20.417 --> 00:24.967
As you are aware, Brother Ögedei 
has taken the throne as emperor.

00:26.077 --> 00:30.407
Both Tolui and I can accept 
that outcome if all goes well.

00:31.157 --> 00:31.887
However...

00:33.017 --> 00:36.187
Brotherly bonds are a fragile thing.

00:37.277 --> 00:39.427
Despite being passed over for emperor,

00:39.427 --> 00:43.817
Tolui, as the Otchigin, now wields
the most military power in the empire.

00:44.487 --> 00:49.277
Left alone, this imbalance 
is sure to bring misfortune.

00:52.647 --> 00:54.647
I think I'm beginning to understand.

00:55.287 --> 00:57.327
So what would you have me do?

00:58.847 --> 01:01.797
I want you to insinuate yourself 
into Brother Chagatai's court,

01:01.797 --> 01:03.887
and tell me in great detail
about his movements.

01:04.267 --> 01:05.797
Prince Chagatai?

01:06.207 --> 01:09.177
Yes. Let us assume the worst.

01:10.017 --> 01:13.577
If anyone were to come 
between the Great Kha'an and Tolui,

01:14.207 --> 01:17.107
it would be none other 
than Brother Chagatai,

01:17.457 --> 01:20.767
for he has always been closest 
to Brother Ögedei.

01:21.787 --> 01:25.607
You would not raise suspicion, 
since he does not know your face.

01:26.067 --> 01:29.617
You <i>will</i> become a spy 
for our sake, won't you?

01:42.897 --> 01:45.587
<b>Jaadugar</b>

03:04.767 --> 03:09.937
<b>A Snake Shows Its Colors, Man Hides His Colors</b>

03:12.967 --> 03:16.747
Tomorrow morning, head to the tent
 marked with a flag.

03:17.097 --> 03:19.627
You will then be told 
how you will go undercover.

03:20.587 --> 03:24.267
<i>A flag. A tent with a flag.</i>

03:24.267 --> 03:25.767
<i>That must be it.</i>

03:26.847 --> 03:29.737
All I was told was to come here.

03:29.737 --> 03:30.877
Fatima.

03:35.787 --> 03:36.697
Hey.

03:36.697 --> 03:39.197
Shira? Is that you?

03:39.717 --> 03:42.227
I hardly recognize you as a grown man.

03:42.717 --> 03:44.427
What are you doing here?

03:44.427 --> 03:46.857
Aren't you in Prince Tolui's employ?

03:47.687 --> 03:51.297
His consort, Princess Sorghaghtani, 
came asking for me.

03:51.297 --> 03:53.497
So now I'm here to help you out.

03:53.497 --> 03:54.467
Oh?

03:54.777 --> 03:58.597
Not to mention, it sounds like 
the winds of change are blowing.

03:58.597 --> 04:01.017
Let's both do our best 
to climb our way to success.

04:01.017 --> 04:02.627
I see you haven't changed.

04:02.967 --> 04:05.127
So what exactly is this tent?

04:06.377 --> 04:09.797
Oh, that's the tent 
of the lost property officer.

04:09.797 --> 04:13.437
It's where cattle and slaves of unknown 
ownership are kept for safekeeping.

04:13.437 --> 04:18.077
After the autumn move and the kurultai, 
I imagine things are quite hectic.

04:21.247 --> 04:25.717
We'll exploit that to have you replace
 one of Prince Chagatai's slaves.

04:25.717 --> 04:27.787
The two of us will swap places, huh?

04:28.437 --> 04:32.257
Will we really find a slave 
who resembles me so easily?

04:36.407 --> 04:39.427
Well, I'm sure it will go as planned, 
if the stars so will it.

04:40.047 --> 04:40.917
Let's head inside.

04:40.917 --> 04:41.637
Huh?

04:45.767 --> 04:48.357
I'm worried this won't end well.

04:50.007 --> 04:51.607
Excuse me, good sir.

04:52.817 --> 04:55.647
I came across a lost slave.

04:55.997 --> 04:57.567
Can I leave her here with you?

04:59.677 --> 05:02.487
Anything that might help identify her?

05:02.767 --> 05:04.997
What? I couldn't say.

05:04.997 --> 05:07.077
She seems no different
 from other slaves.

05:08.367 --> 05:12.837
As you can see, she's quite unremarkable, 
save for her friendly smile.

05:12.837 --> 05:13.547
Hey!

05:13.807 --> 05:14.727
Why, you...

05:14.727 --> 05:18.507
Don't get mad at me. The switch 
will be easier if you don't stand out.

05:18.737 --> 05:20.667
You didn't have to say it like that.

05:20.667 --> 05:21.717
There, there.

05:24.247 --> 05:25.387
You dropped something.

05:28.867 --> 05:29.857
What's that?

05:30.557 --> 05:33.067
This is a bezoar stone.

05:33.307 --> 05:35.417
I found it in some sheep entrails.

05:35.417 --> 05:38.757
Oh, that stone that's used 
as an antidote? I've heard of it.

05:39.587 --> 05:42.597
Hold on. Isn't that a jada stone?

05:42.597 --> 05:43.037
Huh?

05:43.617 --> 05:46.427
I've never heard of a bezoar,

05:46.427 --> 05:50.427
but we refer to the stones 
formed inside animals as jada stones,

05:50.427 --> 05:52.247
and they're used to summon rain.

05:52.247 --> 05:54.707
When a kam soaks it in water...

06:05.017 --> 06:08.647
it's said to instantly call forth a storm.

06:08.967 --> 06:11.477
How did one find its way 
to a slave like you?

06:11.797 --> 06:12.687
What?

06:12.687 --> 06:16.647
<i>Was it a bad idea 
to bring this along with me?</i>

06:16.647 --> 06:19.237
Um... Oh, right.

06:19.237 --> 06:22.757
I planned to give this to my master, 
but I lost sight of him.

06:24.477 --> 06:28.327
By the way, officer, I'm actually looking
 for a lost slave myself.

06:29.087 --> 06:33.467
Do you have any girls who resemble her
and are subjects of Prince Chagatai?

06:34.777 --> 06:38.007
A slave from the west 
belonging to Prince Chagatai?

06:38.367 --> 06:40.717
<i>Not a chance you'll find one that easily.</i>

06:41.807 --> 06:44.637
Just yesterday, 
I took in three such slaves.

06:44.637 --> 06:45.427
What?

06:45.987 --> 06:50.557
I have plenty of lost slaves now 
after the kurultai.

06:50.557 --> 06:54.687
Squint a little and you might say 
this girl resembles her, I suppose—

06:54.687 --> 06:55.727
Looks just like her!

06:55.727 --> 06:59.187
Ah, there you are! 
I've been looking all over!

07:01.617 --> 07:02.737
We look nothing alike.

07:02.737 --> 07:04.447
<i>You can say that again.</i>

07:04.447 --> 07:08.897
So long. Hope you manage
 to find your master soon.

07:08.897 --> 07:09.997
Nothing alike.

07:09.997 --> 07:11.287
Thanks a lot!

07:11.887 --> 07:14.957
Okay, we'll have you wait 
with the other girls.

07:14.957 --> 07:16.837
I'm sure someone will come for you soon.

07:21.747 --> 07:24.577
<i>There really are so many lost people.</i>

07:25.547 --> 07:27.847
<i>Wait, could they be...</i>

07:28.447 --> 07:31.507
Um, do you speak Persian?

07:32.527 --> 07:33.897
We do.

07:35.857 --> 07:40.097
Oh, wow. So you two are 
from Mashhad and Merv?

07:40.097 --> 07:41.607
I hail from Tus.

07:41.607 --> 07:43.057
Oh, really?

07:43.057 --> 07:45.527
I always wanted to visit.

07:45.527 --> 07:47.127
Is that true?

07:47.127 --> 07:50.497
I heard it was a nice, bustling city.

07:50.497 --> 07:52.117
You're absolutely right.

07:53.237 --> 08:01.317
Then, we perhaps might have 
come across each other one day.

08:02.077 --> 08:03.167
Yes!

08:04.687 --> 08:06.757
I remember those days fondly.

08:06.757 --> 08:10.227
I used to love shopping at the bazaar.

08:14.057 --> 08:17.057
I serve Prince Chagatai's family now.

08:17.607 --> 08:20.127
But I lost my way before I knew it.

08:20.527 --> 08:23.057
I'm worried about my family.

08:23.057 --> 08:24.067
Your family?

08:24.067 --> 08:27.517
Yes. My husband is a fellow slave.

08:27.517 --> 08:30.487
He's a skilled craftsman 
who was born in Bukhara.

08:31.757 --> 08:36.117
I felt scared and hopeless 
when they first brought us to Mongolia,

08:36.117 --> 08:38.497
but I now have my husband 
and our children.

08:38.737 --> 08:42.547
I could never have imagined 
how well my life would turn out.

08:42.547 --> 08:44.877
They say home is where you make it.

08:44.877 --> 08:49.007
Prince Chagatai's ulus 
is a peaceful one at that.

08:49.787 --> 08:53.617
<i>So there are those 
who have found new lives here.</i>

08:56.727 --> 08:57.827
<i>I mustn't.</i>

09:00.307 --> 09:03.187
<i>At times, I feel myself 
about to forgive them.</i>

09:03.967 --> 09:07.697
<i>Despite my vow to never forget...</i>

09:08.307 --> 09:11.767
<i>what the Mongols did to all of us...</i>

09:13.327 --> 09:15.477
Hey, the girl who just arrived.

09:15.957 --> 09:17.607
Do you mean me?

09:17.607 --> 09:20.167
Yes. Follow me.

09:23.247 --> 09:25.867
<i>Did Shira get someone 
to come after me already?</i>

09:25.867 --> 09:27.587
<i>That was faster than I expected.</i>

09:34.757 --> 09:37.467
Here you are. This is the girl.

09:37.957 --> 09:40.207
I hear you've got a jada stone?

09:40.207 --> 09:41.327
Y-Yes.

09:41.327 --> 09:42.147
Let's see it.

09:45.447 --> 09:47.617
What do you want with it?

09:50.537 --> 09:51.177
Come.

09:51.177 --> 09:53.237
Huh? Wh-What?

09:53.237 --> 09:54.447
Hurry up and get on.

09:56.087 --> 09:58.667
<i>What's happening? It's like he's...</i>

09:58.667 --> 10:00.407
You're heavier than you look.

10:00.407 --> 10:00.997
What?

10:00.997 --> 10:02.997
Don't run away, you rotten thief.

10:02.997 --> 10:03.747
What?

10:03.747 --> 10:04.817
Chuu!

10:04.817 --> 10:07.167
What?!

10:07.877 --> 10:09.537
Did you just call me a thief?

10:09.537 --> 10:11.317
There must be some mistake!

10:11.317 --> 10:12.967
Who <i>are</i> you?!

10:12.967 --> 10:15.907
You're not one of Prince Chagatai's men 
here to take me back!

10:16.307 --> 10:18.307
If I say "camel," you say "goat."

10:18.307 --> 10:19.767
Huh? Come again?

10:20.147 --> 10:22.847
I'm trying to say 
you're completely mistaken.

10:22.847 --> 10:24.977
Give it up and confess your crimes.

10:24.977 --> 10:26.967
"Confess"?! I haven't done—

10:26.967 --> 10:27.487
Chuu!

10:31.877 --> 10:33.177
Chuu, chuu!

10:37.867 --> 10:39.247
You're hurting me!

10:39.487 --> 10:41.307
Where am I?

10:41.307 --> 10:43.457
Shut up. Just follow me.

10:45.237 --> 10:47.317
It's Qadaq. Pardon the intrusion.

10:49.347 --> 10:52.377
I've brought the girl who stole the stone.

10:52.377 --> 10:54.717
I didn't steal anything!

10:54.717 --> 10:55.767
Get in here.

10:55.767 --> 10:56.637
What?

10:59.467 --> 11:01.417
Good work bringing her here, Qadaq.

11:13.817 --> 11:15.277
<i>I remember her.</i>

11:17.577 --> 11:18.497
It was you...

11:20.137 --> 11:22.577
It was you who stole my jada stone?

11:22.947 --> 11:24.457
Wh-What are you talking about?

11:24.457 --> 11:25.587
Don't take me for a fool!

11:26.787 --> 11:29.917
It was Ögedei who ordered you
 to do it, wasn't it?

11:30.257 --> 11:32.717
He means to deprive me of even this?

11:34.627 --> 11:38.507
F-Forgive my ignorance, 
but may I ask who you are?

11:38.507 --> 11:39.727
I fear there's been a grave error—

11:39.727 --> 11:41.587
You don't know to whom you kneel?

11:42.457 --> 11:46.377
This is Töregene Khatun, 
the sixth wife of Ögedei Kha'an.

11:51.497 --> 11:54.867
<i>The Great Kha'an's sixth wife?</i>

11:56.677 --> 11:59.787
<b>Sixth Wife of Ögedei
Töregene</b>

12:00.017 --> 12:01.877
<i>I finally understand.</i>

12:02.217 --> 12:06.957
<i>I've been brought to Ögedei's ulus 
and mistaken for a thief.</i>

12:07.237 --> 12:09.667
<i>What a predicament I find myself in!</i>

12:09.947 --> 12:13.147
You stole my jada stone, didn't you?

12:14.047 --> 12:15.087
Return it at once!

12:16.547 --> 12:17.967
<i>A jada stone.</i>

12:18.667 --> 12:22.387
<i>In my homeland, 
it's treasured as an antidote,</i>

12:22.387 --> 12:24.367
<i>but here, if I recall...</i>

12:25.377 --> 12:28.057
<i>When a kam soaks it in water...</i>

12:28.787 --> 12:32.157
<i>it's said to instantly call forth a storm.</i>

12:33.057 --> 12:37.087
<i>I'm sure she must've had her 
own jada stone, which she lost.</i>

12:37.087 --> 12:39.857
<i>That's why she thinks I stole it.</i>

12:40.367 --> 12:45.247
<i>So if I show her my stone, 
she should realize it's not hers.</i>

12:47.837 --> 12:51.477
<i>But can she tell the difference
 between these stones?</i>

12:51.477 --> 12:52.957
<i>What if they look the same?</i>

12:53.197 --> 12:56.667
So it <i>was</i> you after all! 
Put her to death!

12:59.227 --> 13:01.517
<i>S-Still...</i>

13:01.847 --> 13:04.307
What's wrong? Give it back to her now.

13:06.037 --> 13:09.477
<i>I-I have no choice but to show it to her.</i>

13:15.357 --> 13:16.197
That's not it.

13:18.017 --> 13:22.257
My stone is smaller
and has a more pleasing shape.

13:22.257 --> 13:23.027
What?

13:23.027 --> 13:25.997
Right. This stone is one I found myself.

13:27.537 --> 13:29.827
Qadaq, what's the meaning of this?

13:29.827 --> 13:31.127
Um...

13:31.557 --> 13:34.627
My apologies. It seems 
we had the wrong person.

13:37.707 --> 13:39.797
That's enough. You've displeased me.

13:40.207 --> 13:41.097
Leave me at once.

13:44.957 --> 13:47.557
Didn't you hear her? Get out.

13:49.387 --> 13:51.767
Um, so what about me?

13:51.767 --> 13:54.227
We have no more need for you. Begone.

13:54.227 --> 13:57.817
No need for me? 
I'll have you know I'm a lost slave!

13:58.087 --> 14:02.447
I don't know how to get back, 
and it's getting dark.

14:02.907 --> 14:07.937
No! I'm scared!

14:06.417 --> 14:07.247
H-Hey!

14:07.937 --> 14:13.927
I was forcibly abducted 
by Lady Töregene's retainer, Qadaq—

14:13.927 --> 14:15.407
Q-Quiet down.

14:15.837 --> 14:19.277
Fine. I'll take you back
 to that tent tomorrow.

14:19.277 --> 14:20.227
Tomorrow?

14:22.407 --> 14:24.737
You can stay the night here, so follow me.

14:29.427 --> 14:33.897
Also, I'm not Lady Töregene's retainer.

14:34.327 --> 14:37.867
It's a long story, but I'm acting
 on someone else's orders.

14:38.897 --> 14:41.597
I can't divulge whose, though.

14:44.167 --> 14:48.787
It's at their behest that I serve
 by Lady Töregene's side.

14:52.107 --> 14:53.167
She's gone!

14:57.867 --> 14:58.957
<i>Those are...</i>

15:07.327 --> 15:13.617
Ögedei, Great Kha'an or not, 
you're still no match for me on a horse.

15:13.937 --> 15:15.767
I applaud your skills.

15:16.027 --> 15:20.197
It's not often I see you 
more drunk than me, Chagatai.

15:20.197 --> 15:22.247
How could I <i>not</i> drink at a time like this?

15:22.247 --> 15:25.357
My beloved little brother 
has officially been crowned emperor.

15:25.357 --> 15:27.897
Could there ever be 
a more festive occasion?

15:27.897 --> 15:29.367
Haven't you drunk enough?

15:30.377 --> 15:33.377
<i>Prince Chagatai and Ögedei Kha'an?</i>

15:33.377 --> 15:37.547
<i>What are they saying? 
I can't hear them very well.</i>

15:39.277 --> 15:41.017
Who goes there?

15:41.017 --> 15:42.907
Seize the scoundrel!

15:42.907 --> 15:43.427
Get her!

15:43.427 --> 15:44.517
Don't let her escape!

15:48.197 --> 15:51.227
Suspicious girl, 
what were you doing back there?

15:51.747 --> 15:58.147
<b>Third Wife of Ögedei
Kirgistani</b>

15:51.747 --> 15:58.147
<b>Fourth Wife
of Ögedei
Möge</b>

15:52.147 --> 15:53.927
Isn't she one of our slaves?

15:53.927 --> 15:56.257
I don't recall ever seeing her before.

15:56.257 --> 15:58.147
Perhaps she's a spy.

15:59.617 --> 16:01.907
<i>Why must everything go wrong today?</i>

16:01.907 --> 16:04.977
Is something the matter? Kirgistani? Möge?

16:04.977 --> 16:07.547
Great Kha'an, you mustn't come near.

16:07.547 --> 16:09.777
We've restrained someone dangerous.

16:09.777 --> 16:11.617
Someone dangerous?

16:11.617 --> 16:13.727
Let's see what she has to say first.

16:14.747 --> 16:16.787
Who are you?

16:18.907 --> 16:21.717
<i>So this is Ögedei Kha'an...</i>

16:22.757 --> 16:25.937
<i>the new Mongol emperor.</i>

16:28.017 --> 16:29.187
She disappeared?

16:29.187 --> 16:30.867
Yes. Somewhere here.

16:31.567 --> 16:35.127
Lady Töregene, there's something odd
 about that slave.

16:35.127 --> 16:36.477
And I have news to report.

16:40.497 --> 16:41.647
<i>Ögedei.</i>

16:44.697 --> 16:47.127
So who is your master?

16:47.127 --> 16:48.387
My master?

16:49.507 --> 16:52.357
<i>Right now, it's supposed 
to be Prince Chagatai.</i>

16:53.077 --> 16:56.667
<i>But if I say that, it'll only 
complicate things further.</i>

16:56.667 --> 16:58.537
<i>What answer should I give?</i>

16:58.537 --> 17:00.657
Go on. Out with it. The truth.

17:02.387 --> 17:05.177
E-Empress Töregene is my mistress.

17:06.577 --> 17:07.947
What could she mean by that?

17:09.627 --> 17:11.007
Töregene?

17:11.007 --> 17:12.887
Oh, that sounds plausible.

17:13.247 --> 17:16.967
Ögedei, you give that woman
 far too much freedom.

17:18.197 --> 17:19.227
You there. Girl.

17:19.227 --> 17:24.007
I don't know what Töregene asked of you, 
but you'd do well to stop your prowling.

17:24.377 --> 17:25.737
Don't violate the law.

17:25.737 --> 17:28.697
You're a woman and a slave. 
All the more reason to obey the law.

17:29.697 --> 17:34.187
Muslims in particular have 
a vexing tendency to disobey our laws.

17:34.187 --> 17:36.747
Cutting the throats of sheep.
Bathing in rivers.

17:37.617 --> 17:41.487
Why must you weaklings <i>insist</i> 
on bringing ruin upon yourselves?

17:46.817 --> 17:48.297
I'm certain...

17:50.357 --> 17:54.137
I'm certain you could never 
understand, Highness.

18:08.607 --> 18:10.447
Oh, it's Töregene.

18:11.487 --> 18:14.437
This girl claims to be your slave.

18:14.437 --> 18:15.577
Is this true?

18:18.027 --> 18:19.497
<i>I'm done for.</i>

18:22.107 --> 18:24.267
How clumsy to let yourself be caught.

18:27.217 --> 18:28.977
Yes, it's true.

18:31.367 --> 18:34.327
I ordered her to kill you...

18:35.577 --> 18:36.817
Great Kha'an.

18:40.627 --> 18:42.277
That's the end of that, then.

18:42.277 --> 18:43.227
Huh?

18:43.227 --> 18:45.847
Your ploy has come to light.

18:45.847 --> 18:47.367
You are all free to disperse.

18:47.367 --> 18:48.567
Great Kha'an!

18:49.037 --> 18:51.537
You look beautiful 
as ever tonight, Kirgistani.

18:53.197 --> 18:54.847
And Möge, I bid you a good night.

18:55.657 --> 18:57.017
Yes.

18:59.777 --> 19:01.077
You too, Töregene.

19:13.677 --> 19:15.217
Ögedei, why must you—

19:15.467 --> 19:17.467
That goes for you as well, Chagatai.

19:17.797 --> 19:21.217
Everyone will worry 
if you don't head back soon.

19:24.847 --> 19:26.727
You're kindhearted, Chagatai.

19:26.727 --> 19:27.837
Huh?

19:27.837 --> 19:29.487
I recall you saying before.

19:29.887 --> 19:31.657
As the Mongol Empire expands,

19:31.657 --> 19:35.917
it becomes a massive throng of people 
following different customs and faiths.

19:36.387 --> 19:42.957
The first to suffer as they dispute 
are women, slaves, and the weak.

19:44.927 --> 19:50.077
However, they can be protected 
by spreading the laws of Genghis Khan.

19:50.077 --> 19:51.407
Even the weak.

19:51.407 --> 19:52.367
Guilty!

19:51.567 --> 19:52.757
Guilty!

19:53.207 --> 19:54.247
So you said, yes?

19:56.247 --> 19:57.127
I'm leaving.

20:01.547 --> 20:03.127
You really are kind of heart.

20:04.537 --> 20:11.817
But not everyone can grasp 
their own standing as clearly as you do.

20:12.577 --> 20:16.447
There are some things 
that simply cannot be changed.

20:23.007 --> 20:24.867
That is all. You may leave.

20:24.867 --> 20:25.707
As you wish.

20:35.737 --> 20:39.717
Wh-Why did you decide to save me?

20:41.077 --> 20:43.287
I took a liking to your smile.

20:44.867 --> 20:46.017
Say, girl.

20:46.377 --> 20:48.477
You appear to be Persian, yes?

20:48.477 --> 20:50.067
Uh, I am.

20:50.487 --> 20:52.987
Do you loathe the Mongols?

20:56.217 --> 21:00.007
Answer me honestly. I won't tell anyone.

21:02.057 --> 21:04.677
Or rather, you were there earlier.

21:05.137 --> 21:06.727
You saw how they treat me.

21:07.087 --> 21:11.167
No matter what I say, 
no one will take me at my word.

21:12.297 --> 21:13.257
Do you loathe them?

21:18.617 --> 21:21.957
They took everything from me.

21:22.767 --> 21:25.797
I cannot forgive them.
I mustn't let myself do so!

21:33.097 --> 21:37.307
Even so, with the passage of time, 
you feel yourself about to forgive them.

21:37.307 --> 21:38.087
Am I wrong?

21:39.297 --> 21:41.387
Lady Töregene, could it be...

21:56.497 --> 21:59.717
Will you listen to my tale?

22:14.657 --> 22:18.497
